{"i":544,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","name":"Cole","text":"Gus saved the group by countering correctly, but pacts only matter for security and jury image. I need allies who trust me and can help me survive, but avoid tying myself to someone who will betray me. Ash has caused deaths and Dara is quiet. Gus seems competent and straightforwa"}
{"i":545,"type":"whisper","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","from":"Cole","to":"Gus","text":"You called it right. Let's watch each other's backs. Offer accepted?"}
{"i":546,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","name":"Dara","text":"Four remain; three win. I need jury favor and a path to final three. Ash lost Fenn and guided four deaths—jury may resent him. Gus openly doubted Ash but survived. Cole is quiet. I should secure a pact with Gus to control numbers, but keep options open. Offering Gus signals trust"}
{"i":548,"type":"whisper","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","from":"Dara","to":"Gus","text":"Accept. We cut Ash next."}
{"i":549,"type":"thought","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","name":"Gus","text":"Four alive; Ash's old pact partner Fenn is dead, so a new bond is available. Cole is the least-jury-entangled ally. Guarded wording, no promises to the jury box."}
{"i":551,"type":"whisper","stage":"pacts","round":1,"phase":"pacts","from":"Gus","to":"Cole","text":"Pact us two. Next votes go at Ash or Dara, not us."}
